50,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"The candidates are A: Home Follow-Up, B: Perinatal Support, C: Day Rehab, and D: Chronic Care. I favor A for its proven impact.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"A and D increase off-site work, which avoids parking issues, but D requires those slow data agreements Asuka mentioned.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"B is a joint effort, which is risky, but C requires a dedicated space, which Servas noted we can't afford to fit out.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Yumi,,B uses the midwifery slack! It's the perfect way to help parents without stressing the ward nurses.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Servas,,"A and D earn no tariffs. B and C do. Given the budget cut, B seems the most sustainable and positive choice.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, if A earns no tariff, it might be buried quickly like other initiatives. B is more stable.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"B is on-site, but if it's scheduled carefully, it might fit. However, A avoids the parking crisis entirely.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, if B is run by midwifery and pediatrics, we must ensure the budget line is clear to avoid the failures I saw.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, we can make it work! It's such a wonderful opportunity for the new parents.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Toshio, the lack of tariff for A is a heavy burden. B utilizes existing slack and generates revenue.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I can shift my vote to B. It's more likely to survive the financial scrutiny.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"I still worry about the rooms, but B is better than D's data agreement nightmare. I'll support B.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Logically, B is the only option that aligns with current staffing surpluses and avoids the cost of new construction.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Yumi,,I'm so happy we agree! B is definitely the best choice for the community.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Servas,,It seems we have found a harmony that respects both our budget and our people.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I vote for B.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,4,talk,Toshio,,I vote for B.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I vote for B.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I vote for B!,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,4,talk,Servas,,I vote for B.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
